{"ts":"2026-08-31T20:10:34.861Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"5d96ff5dd6a189ca37b8b865","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Ported from the pm-todos reference (read, not copied): scripts/shell-command-scan.ts, scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts, test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts. Each fix gets an audit-level failing fixture paired with a genuinely attested sibling publish, a revert-red check, and mirror-direction guards so narrowing never blinds the scan."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-jira-hsjx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Five fail-open publish-attestation bypasses in the vendored shell scan"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm-todos closed five fail-open bypasses in its vendored shell-command-scan / verify-release-publish-attestation pair. Port each into pm-jira's own structure on PR 82, proving every one by behaviour: failing fixture first, fix, then revert-red. Bypasses: (1) heredoc bodies invent bindings; (2) escaped separators invent attestation; (3) file-wide scalar resolution lets a later assignment attest an earlier publish; (4) a backslash-quoted heredoc delimiter never matches its terminator; (5) scope-blind expansion credits out-of-scope bindings to a publish."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-31T20:10:34.861Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T20:10:34.861Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-agent"}],"before_hash":"