{"ts":"2026-08-31T20:42:44.255Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"2e37782ad60a9b8410683521","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T20:42:44.255Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-31T20:42:44.255Z","author":"claude","text":"Two follow-ups after the agent pass. First, the tracker item had been written with the globally installed pm 2026.8.31 while this repository pinned 2026.8.28, and 2026.8.31 writes item_hash_version 3 which 2026.8.28 cannot read at all: pm health failed with unsupported_item_hash_version:3 at gate_failing. Measured the boundary directly, 2026.8.24 and 2026.8.28 both write epoch 2 and 2026.8.31 writes 3, so this is a hard forward-compatibility break rather than the drift class. Resolved by converging this repository's pin on 2026.8.31 like the rest of the fleet. Second, the case-arm bypass was found after the porting pass began and so was missing here: a case arm label ends in a bare closing parenthesis that the generic depth counter read as a group close, dropping the depth so an assignment inside an untaken arm was tagged file-scoped and attested a publish after esac. Ported the case-aware depth counter and verified all eight bypasses plus three in-scope mirror cases behave correctly."}]}],"before_hash":"dd1fa1f02a8b1857fcfde3bc3afb9378ba601fb2f5fb03ae6e4ffde7ca070ebd","after_hash":"8a6a164e5d30fb40972083f9fba61d791055595788efb1bd3404bf5ff842b51d","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
